practice_explanation = "In O(n + k), n is the number of elements and k is the RANGE of possible values. For example, if you're sorting scores from 0-100, k = 101. If sorting ages 0-120, k = 121. Counting Sort is fast when k is small (like 100 or 256) but becomes slow when k is huge (like millions of unique values)."
